    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "East Palo Alto Academy (EPAA) is a small public charter high school in the Sequoia Union High School District. For our 2023-2024 POLS Field Project, we aimed to identify why EPAA students failed to engage regularly with the school’s College and Career Center resources. Through our focus group discussions, survey results, and interviews with key staff, we identified four factors that motivated students to participate in enrichment activities. In addition, we identified four implementation areas that EPAA could address to improve the organization of enrichment activities. With our findings, we developed two frameworks to support EPAA: SAIL Student Motivation Framework and Four ‘Ps’ Implementation Framework. To improve student engagement with enrichment activities, we recommended that EPAA revisit the implementation and organization of its enrichment activities while considering the student archetypes to ensure that the program objectives align with student interests.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Suppiah, J. and Chavez, J. (2024). Apathetic or Disengaged: Why are East Palo Alto Academy (EPAA) Students Not Participating in Enrichment Activities?. Stanford Digital Repository. Available at https://purl.stanford.edu/sh545rz5207. https://doi.org/10.25740/sh545rz5207.",
            "type": "preferred citation",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        }
